   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Thanks for the help, final code for matching Excel:</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div class=\"gmail_default\">df &lt;- data.frame(Condition = c(&quot;Control&quot;, &quot;Experimental&quot;), Complied = c(&quot;Complied&quot;, &quot;Complied&quot;,&quot;Did Not Comply&quot;, &quot;Did Not Comply&quot;), Compliance = c(0.77, 0.29, 0.23, 0.71))</div><div class=\"gmail_default\">ggplot(data = df, aes(x = Complied, y = Compliance, fill = Condition)) + geom_bar(stat = &quot;identity&quot;, position = &quot;dodge&quot;) + scale_x_discrete(name = &quot;&quot;)</div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br></div><div><br></div><br>Best,<div>Timothy</div><div><br><br><br><font color=\"#cccccc\">&quot;The will to win means nothing without the will to prepare.&quot;</font><br><div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juma_Ikangaa\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juma_Ikangaa&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369482256000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NrKg7zOKcuOdYricsCkR5\"><font color=\"#9fc5e8\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juma_Ikangaa</font></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\">\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Mar 6, 2015 at 12:39 PM, Mark Lyman <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mark....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Something like this maybe<br>library(plyr)<br>library(reshape2)<br>library(ggplot2)<br><br>df &lt;- data.frame(Condition = factor(c(1, 0), levels = c(1, 0), labels = c(&quot;Experimental&quot;, &quot;Control&quot;)), Complied = c(.77, .29))<br><br>df &lt;- melt(mutate(df, `Did Not Comply` = 1 - Complied))<br><br>p &lt;- ggplot(data = df, aes(x = variable, y = value)) # bar plot<br>p +<br>  geom_bar(aes(fill = Condition), stat = &quot;identity&quot;, position = &quot;dodge&quot;) +<br>  scale_fill_manual(values = c(&quot;blue&quot;, &quot;red&quot;)) +<br>  theme_bw() +<br>  theme(title = element_blank())<div><div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Mar 6, 2015 at 10:22 AM Ben Bond-Lamberty &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bpb...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Currently there&#39;s not enough information in your sample data frame (two values) to reproduce the Excel graph (four values). You probably want to do something like this:<div><br></div><div>df &lt;- data.frame(Condition=c(&quot;Control&quot;, &quot;Experimental&quot;), Compliance=c(&quot;Complied&quot;, &quot;Complied&quot;,&quot;Did Not Comply&quot;, &quot;Did Not Comply&quot;), value=c(0.77, 0.29, 0.23, 0.71))<br></div><div>ggplot(df,aes(Compliance, value, fill=Condition))+geom_bar(stat=&quot;identity&quot;, position=&quot;dodge&quot;)<br></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>Ben</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Mar 6, 2015 at 12:04 PM, Timothy Lau <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">timoth...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">I&#39;m having trouble reproducing a graph in ggplot that I made in Excel.</span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><br></span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">In Excel the graph looks like this</span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><br></span></span></div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><img style=\"border-style:none\" alt=\"bargraph.png\" height=\"192\" width=\"320\"></span></span><br><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><br></span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">In R it looks like this</span></span></div><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-B49CaXmOcmM/VPnUNHw7UQI/AAAAAAAB2bU/FliNyHwf5Zc/s1600/Rplot04.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-B49CaXmOcmM/VPnUNHw7UQI/AAAAAAAB2bU/FliNyHwf5Zc/s1600/Rplot04.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369482256000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0TxkdzWsI5Ky3pC3oRLl02\"><img border=\"0\" height=\"268\" width=\"400\"></a></p><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><br></span></span></div><div><br></div><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">Here&#39;s my code:</span></span></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\"><div style=\"font-size:15px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><i>df &lt;- data.frame(Condition = factor(c(1, 0), levels = c(1, 0), labels = c(&quot;Experimental&quot;, &quot;Control&quot;)), Compliance = c(.77, .29))</i></div></font></span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\"><div><span style=\"font-size:15px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><i>p &lt;- ggplot(data = df, aes(x = Condition, y = Compliance)) # bar plot</i></span></div></font></span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\"><div><span style=\"font-size:15px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><i>p + geom_bar(stat = &quot;identity&quot;, fill = c(4,2))</i></span></div></font></span></span></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">I want to know how to get R to split the columns like the Excel example using just my data frame &quot;df&quot;</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:15px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\"><div>        Condition         Compliance</div><div>1      Experimental   0.77</div></font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial;font-size:15px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">2      Control            0.29</span> </div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n