   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>What is Excel?<br><br></div>Unfortunately many organisations use Excel for storing data.  Store data in a database and use Excel for calculations.<br><br></div>You may be better off with R or Python.<br><br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On 6 March 2015 at 17:41, Scott Tetrick <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">scottt...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">you don&#39;t quite have everything in your data frame, and certain you have more Excel data.  You will want to look at things like position=&quot;dodge&quot;, and maybe ?melt in library reshape2.<div><br></div><div>I think your &quot;Did Not Comply&quot; is 1-Complied?  That&#39;s another column even in Excel, and it will be in your df as well.  If you want 4 total bars, your dr needs 4 numbers in it. </div></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Mar 6, 2015 at 10:04 AM, Timothy Lau <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">timoth...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">I&#39;m having trouble reproducing a graph in ggplot that I made in Excel.</span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><br></span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">In Excel the graph looks like this</span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><br></span></span></div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><img src=\"https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/0-Wx22M7UrX1FkvWYnzvBIMZY6sID2FUtI6FtrJgunnJRf-KgG7Svayh2AxrOyrH8r2fDKqiQfXKI7a4K1DRJ0-LuC7nz_h7a-s_ULGLN35Y8zi3khEZLcWvRQKQ_QL4Ptat45A\" style=\"border-style:none\" alt=\"bargraph.png\" height=\"192\" width=\"320\"></span></span><br><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><br></span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">In R it looks like this</span></span></div><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-B49CaXmOcmM/VPnUNHw7UQI/AAAAAAAB2bU/FliNyHwf5Zc/s1600/Rplot04.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-B49CaXmOcmM/VPnUNHw7UQI/AAAAAAAB2bU/FliNyHwf5Zc/s1600/Rplot04.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369482263000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0R09XEck5Gpy90P_mWIKms\"><img src=\"https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-B49CaXmOcmM/VPnUNHw7UQI/AAAAAAAB2bU/FliNyHwf5Zc/s400/Rplot04.png\" border=\"0\" height=\"268\" width=\"400\"></a></p><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><br></span></span></div><div><br></div><div><span><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">Here&#39;s my code:</span></span></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#000000\"><div style=\"font-size:15px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><i>df &lt;- data.frame(Condition = factor(c(1, 0), levels = c(1, 0), labels = c(&quot;Experimental&quot;, &quot;Control&quot;)), Compliance = c(.77, .29))</i></div></font></span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#000000\"><div><span style=\"font-size:15px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><i>p &lt;- ggplot(data = df, aes(x = Condition, y = Compliance)) # bar plot</i></span></div></font></span></span></div><div><span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#000000\"><div><span style=\"font-size:15px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><i>p + geom_bar(stat = &quot;identity&quot;, fill = c(4,2))</i></span></div></font></span></span></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-size:15px;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">I want to know how to get R to split the columns like the Excel example using just my data frame &quot;df&quot;</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:15px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#000000\"><div>        Condition         Compliance</div><div>1      Experimental   0.77</div></font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial;font-size:15px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">2      Control            0.29</span> </div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369482263000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07asxYIkjpl5YmjCCnpp1E\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369482263000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vhdZqItc2p3FGZzcummIH\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>\r\n<br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ggplot2&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369482263000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3rA6tKHJdt1rz3TomvlG78\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369482263000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07asxYIkjpl5YmjCCnpp1E\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369482263000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vhdZqItc2p3FGZzcummIH\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>\r\n<br>\r